\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.10}{\ignorespaces \texttt  {\_follow\_line}, the supervisor added around the stock line-follower node. It owns exactly the three things the node has no opinion about: arrival, obstacle stopping through the polled sonar (using \texttt  {\_sonar\_seq} to tell two fresh readings from one stale one read twice), and a wall-clock give-up, since the node itself drives forward indefinitely if the line is lost. The \texttt  {\_lf\_unavailable} check (added 11 October) means a drive that never started is reported as blocked rather than as a drive that ran and found nothing.}}{49}{figure.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:flow-followline}{{5.10}{49}{\texttt {\_follow\_line}, the supervisor added around the stock line-follower node. It owns exactly the three things the node has no opinion about: arrival, obstacle stopping through the polled sonar (using \texttt {\_sonar\_seq} to tell two fresh readings from one stale one read twice), and a wall-clock give-up, since the node itself drives forward indefinitely if the line is lost. The \texttt {\_lf\_unavailable} check (added 11 October) means a drive that never started is reported as blocked rather than as a drive that ran and found nothing}{figure.caption.37}{}}
\newlabel{fig:flow-followline@cref}{{[figure][10][5]5.10}{[1][47][]49}{}{}{}}
